use "emit_c.a0"

# A0 port of the instruction-list post-processing `Code.finish` of src/wasm.ts (DESIGN.md 7a): the
# function body arrives as a list of instructions with SYMBOLIC local indices; `wfzfin` stackifies
# adjacent local.set/local.get pairs, drops dead stores, renumbers the non-parameter locals so that
# ones with disjoint live ranges (widened across loops) share an index, and serializes the list.
# The result is byte-identical to the TypeScript (compiler/wasm_code.a0 is checked against `finish`
# on random lists and on every function body of the test programs).
#
# Input: the table `ins` (u32x128x352: 22528 instructions of 2 words; instruction k is word 2k =
# kind, word 2k+1 = v), the instruction count n and the parameter count np (locals below np are
# never renumbered or removed). The kinds, and the bytes each serializes to (uleb/sleb are the
# LEB128 forms of src/wasm.ts, sleb of the int32 whose bit pattern is v):
#    0 NOP nothing           1 OP v the byte v&255      2 CONST v 0x41 sleb(v)
#    3 LGET v 0x20 uleb(v)   4 LSET v 0x21 uleb(v)      5 LTEE v 0x22 uleb(v)   (v renumbered below np)
#    6 CALL v: one marker word v (>= 256)               7 POOL v: one marker word 2^31 + v
#    8 LOOP 0x03 0x40        9 LOOPEND 0x0b             10 LOAD v 0x28 2 uleb(v)  11 STORE v 0x36 2 uleb(v)
#   12 BRIF v 0x0d uleb(v)  13 BR v 0x0c uleb(v)        14 BLOCK v 0x02 v&255     15 IF v 0x04 v&255
#   16 MEMCOPY 0xfc 0x0a 0 0  17 MEMFILL 0xfc 0x0b 0    18 SIMD v 0xfd uleb(v)    19 VSTORE 0xfd 0x0b 2 0
#   20 VCONSTIDX 0xfd 0x0c then the lanes 0 1 2 3 (u32, little endian)
#   21 VCONSTSPLAT v 0xfd 0x0c then v (little endian) four times
#   22 GGET v 0x23 v&255    23 GSET v 0x24 v&255
# A local id below 2^20 (VBASE) is an i32 local (id < 8192 when not a parameter), an id VBASE + k
# (k < 128) a v128 local; the v128 locals are placed after the i32 ones. A local id outside these
# ranges, more than 22528 instructions, or more than 65533 output words is the failure value.
# Loops (kinds 8, 9) are balanced and nested; blocks and ifs are not loops.
#
# Result (wfzfin): the code table (u32x128x512). Words 0 .. nwords-1 are the body, one word per
# byte plus a marker word for each CALL/POOL; the last three words are the header: word 65533 =
# nwords, the number of words written (4294967295 on failure, then the other two are 0), word
# 65534 = nlocals (the i32 locals above the np parameters) and word 65535 = nvlocals (the v128
# locals), i.e. `locals` and `vlocals` of `Code.finish`. (A record with the table would pass
# the 2^21 bit limit of a value, so the three scalars live in the table: the body holds at most
# 65533 words.)
#
# Method. Every pass is a fold over the instructions whose state is a table (u32x128x512 = 65536
# words, element i at page i>>7, word i&127), updated in place; tables read by a pass are fold
# extras (borrowed, never copied), and a write is a one-trip fold of a tiny body (`wfzp1`, ...).
# 1. wfzcnt: gets and sets per local (a LTEE counts as a set) over the original list.
# 2. wfzstk: stackify on a copy of the list: a set directly followed by a get of the same local
#    vanishes with it (one read, one write) or becomes a tee; a dead set becomes OP 0x1a, a dead
#    tee vanishes. A removed instruction is kind 0; positions stay the original indices.
# 3. wfzrng: per local its first and last access and the top-level (outermost) loop around each;
#    per top-level loop its start and end. Since loops nest, repeated widening against all loops
#    is the hull with the outermost loop around the first access (start) and last access (end).
# 4. wfzalc: the locals in order of first access (the TypeScript stable sort by widened start gives
#    the same order) take the first slot whose end is below the widened start; i32 and v128 locals
#    have separate slot sets; the slot is kept per local.
# 5. wfzoff, wfzcode: the offset of every instruction (running sum of its length), then its
#    bytes, written one by one (wfzbyte).
# The tables start as `wfzz` (all zero) and are laid out as follows (word indices):
#   count table  : gets of local c at c, sets at 8320 + c (c: i32 id, or 8192 + k for VBASE + k),
#                  16640: set to 1 when a local id is out of range, 16641 scratch
#   range table  : 0 loop depth, 1 top-level loop count, 8 9 16..19 scratch, 128 + 4c: first
#                  access + 1, its top-level loop, last access, its top-level loop,
#                  33408 + L: start and 44928 + L: end of top-level loop L
#   slot table   : c: slot of local c, 8320 + s: end of i32 slot s, 16512 + s: end of v128 slot
#                  s, 16640 and 16641: slots used (i32, v128), 16650 and 16651 scratch
#   offset table : word i is the offset of instruction i (n + 1 words)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tables

# word p1 of the table p0
fn wfzg u32x128x512 u32 -> u32
a shr p1 7
b get p0 a
c and p1 127
d get b c
ret d
end
# word p1 of the input list
fn wfzgi u32x128x352 u32 -> u32
a shr p1 7
b get p0 a
c and p1 127
d get b c
ret d
end
# the state with word p2 set to p3 (a fold of one trip: p1 is the trip)
fn wfzp1 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
a shr p2 7
b get p0 a
c and p2 127
d set b c p3
e set p0 a d
ret e
end
# the state with the words p2 and p2 + 1 (same page) set to p3 and p4
fn wfzp2 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
a shr p2 7
b get p0 a
c and p2 127
d set b c p3
e add c 1
f set d e p4
g set p0 a f
ret g
end
# the state with the words p2 .. p2 + 3 (p2 a multiple of 4) set to p3 .. p6
fn wfzp4 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
a shr p2 7
b get p0 a
c and p2 127
d set b c p3
e add c 1
f set d e p4
g add c 2
h set f g p5
i add c 3
j set h i p6
k set p0 a j
ret k
end
# the zero table
fn wfzz -> u32x128x512
a call zpage
b arr a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a
ret b
end
# the zero input list
fn wfzzi -> u32x128x352
a call zpage
b arr a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a
ret b
end
# page p1 of the input list p2 copied into the state (a fold of 352 trips)
fn wfzcp u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x352 -> u32x128x512
a get p2 p1
b set p0 p1 a
ret b
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local ids

# 1 for a local access kind (3 get, 4 set, 5 tee)
fn wfzisl u32 -> bool
a sub p0 3
b lt a 3
ret b
end
# the compact index of local id p0: i32 ids below 8192 as they are, VBASE + k (k < 128) as 8192 + k,
# 0 for an id out of range
fn wfzcidx u32 -> u32
a lt p0 8192
b sub p0 1048576
c lt b 128
d add b 8192
e select c d 0
f select a p0 e
ret f
end
# is local id p0 in range
fn wfzvok u32 -> bool
a lt p0 8192
b sub p0 1048576
c lt b 128
d or a c
ret d
end
# the final index of local id p0 (slot table p0, parameters p1, i32 locals p2): parameters stay,
# an i32 local is np + slot, a v128 local np + nl + slot
fn wfzmap u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 -> u32
a call wfzcidx p3
b shr a 7
c and a 127
d get p0 b
e get d c
f lt p3 8192
g lt p3 p1
h add p1 e
i add p1 p2
j add i e
k select f h j
l select g p3 k
ret l
end
# the operand of an instruction after renumbering: the final index for a local access (kind p3,
# value p4), else p4
fn wfzuse u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32
a call wfzisl p3
b call wfzmap p0 p1 p2 p4
c select a b p4
ret c
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bytes

# bytes of the uleb128 form of p0 (1..5)
fn wfzul u32 -> u32
a ge p0 128
b ge p0 16384
c ge p0 2097152
d ge p0 268435456
e select a 1 0
f select b 1 0
g select c 1 0
h select d 1 0
i add e f
j add i g
k add j h
l add k 1
ret l
end
# bytes of the sleb128 form of the int32 with the bit pattern p0 (1..5)
fn wfzsl u32 -> u32
a add p0 64
b add p0 8192
c add p0 1048576
d add p0 134217728
e ge a 128
f ge b 16384
g ge c 2097152
h ge d 268435456
i select e 1 0
j select f 1 0
k select g 1 0
l select h 1 0
m add i j
n add m k
o add n l
p add o 1
ret p
end
# byte p1 of the uleb128 form of p0
fn wfzuleb u32 u32 -> u32
a call wfzul p0
b add p1 1
c lt b a
d mul p1 7
e shr p0 d
f and e 127
g or f 128
h select c g f
ret h
end
# byte p1 of the sleb128 form of the int32 with the bit pattern p0
fn wfzsleb u32 u32 -> u32
a call wfzsl p0
b add p1 1
c lt b a
d mul p1 7
e shr p0 d
f shr p0 31
g eq f 1
h gt d 0
i and g h
j sub 32 d
k shl 4294967295 j
l select i k 0
m or e l
n and m 127
o or n 128
p select c o n
ret p
end
# length of the fixed prefix of kind p0
fn wfzplen u32 -> u32
a mov 0
b eq p0 2
c select b 1 a
d eq p0 3
e select d 1 c
f eq p0 4
g select f 1 e
h eq p0 5
i select h 1 g
j eq p0 8
k select j 2 i
l eq p0 9
m select l 1 k
n eq p0 10
o select n 2 m
p eq p0 11
q select p 2 o
r eq p0 12
s select r 1 q
t eq p0 13
u select t 1 s
v eq p0 14
w select v 1 u
x eq p0 15
y select x 1 w
z eq p0 16
aa select z 4 y
ab eq p0 17
ac select ab 3 aa
ad eq p0 18
ae select ad 1 ac
af eq p0 19
ag select af 4 ae
ah eq p0 20
ai select ah 2 ag
aj eq p0 21
ak select aj 2 ai
al eq p0 22
am select al 1 ak
an eq p0 23
ao select an 1 am
ret ao
end
# the fixed prefix bytes of kind p0, packed little endian
fn wfzpack u32 -> u32
a mov 0
b eq p0 2
c select b 65 a
d eq p0 3
e select d 32 c
f eq p0 4
g select f 33 e
h eq p0 5
i select h 34 g
j eq p0 8
k select j 16387 i
l eq p0 9
m select l 11 k
n eq p0 10
o select n 552 m
p eq p0 11
q select p 566 o
r eq p0 12
s select r 13 q
t eq p0 13
u select t 12 s
v eq p0 14
w select v 2 u
x eq p0 15
y select x 4 w
z eq p0 16
aa select z 2812 y
ab eq p0 17
ac select ab 3068 aa
ad eq p0 18
ae select ad 253 ac
af eq p0 19
ag select af 134141 ae
ah eq p0 20
ai select ah 3325 ag
aj eq p0 21
ak select aj 3325 ai
al eq p0 22
am select al 35 ak
an eq p0 23
ao select an 36 am
ret ao
end
# length of the variable part of kind p0 whose operand is p1
fn wfzvlen u32 u32 -> u32
a call wfzul p1
b call wfzsl p1
c mov 0
d eq p0 1
e select d 1 c
f eq p0 2
g select f b e
h eq p0 3
i select h a g
j eq p0 4
k select j a i
l eq p0 5
m select l a k
n eq p0 6
o select n 1 m
p eq p0 7
q select p 1 o
r eq p0 10
s select r a q
t eq p0 11
u select t a s
v eq p0 12
w select v a u
x eq p0 13
y select x a w
z eq p0 14
aa select z 1 y
ab eq p0 15
ac select ab 1 aa
ad eq p0 18
ae select ad a ac
af eq p0 20
ag select af 16 ae
ah eq p0 21
ai select ah 16 ag
aj eq p0 22
ak select aj 1 ai
al eq p0 23
am select al 1 ak
ret am
end
# words of the instruction of kind p0 with operand p1 (a local access: its final index)
fn wfzlen u32 u32 -> u32
a call wfzplen p0
b call wfzvlen p0 p1
c add a b
ret c
end
# the variable byte p2 of kind p0 with operand p1 (the index counts from the end of the prefix)
fn wfzvar u32 u32 u32 -> u32
a call wfzuleb p1 p2
b call wfzsleb p1 p2
c and p1 255
d and p2 3
e mul d 8
f shr p1 e
g and f 255
h eq d 0
i shr p2 2
j select h i 0
k add p1 2147483648
l mov 0
m eq p0 1
n select m c l
o eq p0 2
p select o b n
q eq p0 3
r select q a p
s eq p0 4
t select s a r
u eq p0 5
v select u a t
w eq p0 6
x select w p1 v
y eq p0 7
z select y k x
aa eq p0 10
ab select aa a z
ac eq p0 11
ad select ac a ab
ae eq p0 12
af select ae a ad
ag eq p0 13
ah select ag a af
ai eq p0 14
aj select ai c ah
ak eq p0 15
al select ak c aj
am eq p0 18
an select am a al
ao eq p0 20
ap select ao j an
aq eq p0 21
ar select aq g ap
as eq p0 22
au select as c ar
av eq p0 23
aw select av c au
ret aw
end
# word p2 of the instruction of kind p0 with operand p1: a byte, or a marker for a call or a pool address
fn wfzbyte u32 u32 u32 -> u32
a call wfzplen p0
b call wfzpack p0
c lt p2 a
d mul p2 8
e shr b d
f and e 255
g sub p2 a
h call wfzvar p0 p1 g
i select c f h
ret i
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pass 1: counts. State: the count table; trip i: instruction i of p2 (n = p4, np = p3).

# a get of a local adds one to its gets, a set or tee to its sets
fn wfzcnt u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x352 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
a shl p1 1
b call wfzgi p2 a
c add a 1
d call wfzgi p2 c
e call wfzisl b
f ge d p3
g lt p1 p4
h and e f
i and h g
j call wfzcidx d
k call wfzvok d
l eq b 3
m add j 8320
n select l j m
o and i k
p select o 1 0
q shr n 7
r and n 127
s get p0 q
t get s r
u add t p
v eq k false
w and i v
x select w 16640 16641
y shr n 7
z get p0 y
aa and n 127
ab set z aa u
ac set p0 y ab
ad shr x 7
ae get ac ad
af and x 127
ag set ae af 1
ah set ac ad ag
ret ah
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pass 2: stackify. State: the copy of the list; extras: the count table, np, n.

# instruction p1: a set directly followed by a get of the same local (original adjacency) becomes
# nothing together with the get when the local has one get and one set, else a tee; a set whose
# local is never read is OP 0x1a (drop); a tee whose local is never read vanishes. Parameters
# are untouched. A removed instruction is kind 0.
fn wfzstk u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
a shl p1 1
b shr a 7
c and a 127
d get p0 b
e get d c
f add a 1
g shr f 7
h and f 127
i get p0 g
j get i h
k add a 2
l shr k 7
m and k 127
n get p0 l
o get n m
p add a 3
q shr p 7
r and p 127
s get p0 q
t get s r
u call wfzisl e
v ge j p3
w lt p1 p4
x and u v
y and x w
z call wfzcidx j
aa add z 8320
ab shr z 7
ac and z 127
ad get p2 ab
ae get ad ac
af shr aa 7
ag and aa 127
ah get p2 af
ai get ah ag
aj add p1 1
ak lt aj p4
al eq o 3
am eq t j
an and al am
ao and an ak
ap eq e 4
aq eq e 5
ar eq ae 1
as eq ai 1
au and ar as
av eq ae 0
aw select au 0 5
ax select av 1 4
ay select ao aw ax
az select av 26 j
a0 select ao j az
a1 select av 0 5
a2 select aq a1 e
a3 select ap ay a2
a4 select ap a0 j
a5 select y a3 e
a6 select y a4 j
a7 and y ap
a8 and a7 ao
a9 select a8 0 o
ba shr a 7
bb get p0 ba
bc and a 127
bd set bb bc a5
be add bc 1
bf set bd be a6
bg set p0 ba bf
bh shr k 7
bi get bg bh
bj and k 127
bk set bi bj a9
bl set bg bh bk
ret bl
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pass 3: ranges. State: the range table; extras: the stackified list, np.

# instruction p1: loop depth and top-level loops; first and last access of a local
fn wfzrng u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x512 u32 -> u32x128x512
a shl p1 1
b shr a 7
c and a 127
d get p2 b
e get d c
f add a 1
g shr f 7
h and f 127
i get p2 g
j get i h
k shr 0 7
l and 0 127
m get p0 k
n get m l
o shr 1 7
p and 1 127
q get p0 o
r get q p
s eq e 8
t eq e 9
u eq n 0
v and s u
w select v 1 0
x add r w
y eq n 1
z and t y
aa add n 1
ab sub n 1
ac select t ab n
ad select s aa ac
ae gt n 0
af select ae x 0
ag call wfzisl e
ah ge j p3
ai and ag ah
aj call wfzcidx j
ak mul aj 4
al add ak 128
am shr al 7
an and al 127
ao get p0 am
ap get ao an
aq add al 1
ar shr aq 7
as and aq 127
au get p0 ar
av get au as
aw eq ap 0
ax add p1 1
ay select aw ax ap
az select aw af av
a0 select ai al 16
a1 add x 33408
a2 select v a1 8
a3 add r 44928
a4 select z a3 9
a5 shr a0 7
a6 get p0 a5
a7 and a0 127
a8 set a6 a7 ay
a9 add a7 1
ba set a8 a9 az
bb add a7 2
bc set ba bb p1
bd add a7 3
be set bc bd af
bf set p0 a5 be
bg shr 0 7
bh get bf bg
bi and 0 127
bj set bh bi ad
bk add bi 1
bl set bj bk x
bm set bf bg bl
bn shr a2 7
bo get bm bn
bp and a2 127
bq set bo bp p1
br set bm bn bq
bs shr a4 7
bt get br bs
bu and a4 127
bv set bt bu p1
bw set br bs bv
ret bw
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pass 4: slots. State: the slot table; extras: the stackified list, the range table, np.

# slot candidate p0 after slot p1 of the slot table p2 (slot ends from p3 on): the first slot whose
# end is below the start p4, 4294967295 for none yet
fn wfzfit u32 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32 -> u32
a add p3 p1
b shr a 7
c and a 127
d get p2 b
e get d c
f lt e p4
g eq p0 4294967295
h and f g
i select h p1 p0
ret i
end
# instruction p1: at the first access of a local, give it the first free slot of its kind
fn wfzalc u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x512 u32x128x512 u32 -> u32x128x512
a shl p1 1
b shr a 7
c and a 127
d get p2 b
e get d c
f add a 1
g shr f 7
h and f 127
i get p2 g
j get i h
k call wfzisl e
l ge j p4
m and k l
n call wfzcidx j
o mul n 4
p add o 128
q shr p 7
r and p 127
s get p3 q
t get s r
u add p 1
v shr u 7
w and u 127
x get p3 v
y get x w
z add p 2
aa shr z 7
ab and z 127
ac get p3 aa
ad get ac ab
ae add p 3
af shr ae 7
ag and ae 127
ah get p3 af
ai get ah ag
aj add p1 1
ak eq t aj
al and m ak
am eq y 0
an add y 33408
ao shr an 7
ap and an 127
aq get p3 ao
ar get aq ap
as select am p1 ar
au eq ai 0
av add ai 44928
aw shr av 7
ax and av 127
ay get p3 aw
az get ay ax
a0 select au ad az
a1 lt j 8192
a2 select a1 8320 16512
a3 select a1 16640 16641
a4 shr a3 7
a5 and a3 127
a6 get p0 a4
a7 get a6 a5
a8 fold wfzfit a7 4294967295 p0 a2 as
a9 eq a8 4294967295
ba select a9 a7 a8
bb select a9 1 0
bc add a7 bb
bd select al bc a7
be select al n 16650
bf add a2 ba
bg select al bf 16651
bh shr be 7
bi get p0 bh
bj and be 127
bk set bi bj ba
bl set p0 bh bk
bm shr bg 7
bn get bl bm
bo and bg 127
bp set bn bo a0
bq set bl bm bp
br shr a3 7
bs get bq br
bt and a3 127
bu set bs bt bd
bv set bq br bu
ret bv
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pass 5: offsets and bytes

# state: the offset table; instruction p1 of the stackified list p2 starts at word p1 of the
# state, the next at the sum with its length (slot table p3, np p4, i32 locals p5)
fn wfzoff u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x512 u32x128x512 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
a shl p1 1
b shr a 7
c and a 127
d get p2 b
e get d c
f add a 1
g shr f 7
h and f 127
i get p2 g
j get i h
k call wfzuse p3 p4 p5 e j
l call wfzlen e k
m shr p1 7
n and p1 127
o get p0 m
p get o n
q add p l
r add p1 1
s shr r 7
t get p0 s
u and r 127
v set t u q
w set p0 s v
ret w
end
# state: the code table; trip p1 writes word p2 + p1 (the instruction starts at word p2) when p1 is
# below the length p5 of the instruction of kind p3 and operand p4 (a fold of 18 trips: the longest
# instruction is 18 words)
fn wfzbw u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
a add p2 p1
b shr a 7
c and a 127
d get p0 b
e get d c
f call wfzbyte p3 p4 p1
g lt p1 p5
h select g f e
i shr a 7
j get p0 i
k and a 127
l set j k h
m set p0 i l
ret m
end
# state: the code table; instruction p1 of the stackified list p2 (slot table p3, offsets p4, np
# p5, i32 locals p6) written at its offset
fn wfzcode u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x512 u32x128x512 u32x128x512 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
a shl p1 1
b shr a 7
c and a 127
d get p2 b
e get d c
f add a 1
g shr f 7
h and f 127
i get p2 g
j get i h
k call wfzuse p3 p5 p6 e j
l call wfzlen e k
m shr p1 7
n and p1 127
o get p4 m
p get o n
q fold wfzbw 18 p0 p e k l
ret q
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The function

# `Code.finish(np)` of the list p0 of p1 instructions: the code table, whose last three words
# 65533, 65534, 65535 are the words written (4294967295 on failure), the i32 locals and the v128 locals
fn wfzfin u32x128x352 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
a gt p1 22528
b select a 22528 p1
c call wfzz
d fold wfzcp 352 c p0
e call wfzz
f fold wfzcnt b e p0 p2 b
g call wfzz
h fold wfzstk b d f p2 b
i fold wfzrng b g h p2
j call wfzz
k fold wfzalc b j h i p2
l shr 16640 7
m and 16640 127
n get k l
o get n m
p shr 16641 7
q and 16641 127
r get k p
s get r q
t call wfzz
u fold wfzoff b t h k p2 o
v call wfzz
w fold wfzcode b v h k u p2 o
x shr b 7
y and b 127
z get u x
aa get z y
ab shr 16640 7
ac and 16640 127
ad get f ab
ae get ad ac
af eq ae 0
ag le aa 65533
ah and af ag
ai eq a false
aj and ah ai
ak select aj aa 4294967295
al select aj o 0
am select aj s 0
an fold wfzp1 1 w 65533 ak
ao fold wfzp1 1 an 65534 al
ap fold wfzp1 1 ao 65535 am
ret ap
end
